In process_observations (worktree_event_watcher.rs:1335-1405), when the dev-leaf pushes new commits AND the old terminal review is still visible from the Forgejo API in the same poll cycle, the following sequence runs inside the lock:

1. head_sha_changed = true => reviewer_spawned = false; reviewer_disposed = false  (reset)
2. should_spawn_reviewer_for_new_head = true => spawn_reviewer_for_pr called  (correct)
3. terminal_review_observed = true AND !ws.reviewer_disposed (just reset) => reviewer_disposed = true  (stomps the reset)

reviewer_disposed is then true for the remainder of the cycle. The reviewer_disposals list also gets this PR, so dispose_reviewers_for_pr runs and races with the just-spawned reviewer's worktree creation.

The stale_terminal_review_after_head_change flag was designed to handle this but only fires when forgejo_review_present = false. If the old review has no commit_id (passes the SHA filter), or the Forgejo API returns it without one, forgejo_review_present = true and the guard does not trigger.

