## Problem

After #398 removed file-based reviewer state, cleanup_force_reviewer_resources and live_reviewer_for_pr both scan .exo/agents/ and .exo/worktrees/ for reviewer entries. These directories no longer hold reviewer state. Both functions silently return empty results, so cleanup_reviewer_leaf always reports cleaned_reviewers=[] and never kills tmux windows. Confirmed three times in nemotron-port sessions.

## Fix

### 1. Rewrite cleanup_force_reviewer_resources (handlers/agent.rs ~L1523)

Remove: reviewer_resource_slugs_for_pr, collect_reviewer_resource_slugs, is_reviewer_resource_slug_for_pr (dead code)

Replace with tmux window scan:

async fn cleanup_force_reviewer_resources<C>(..., pr_number: u64) -> Vec<String>
where C: ... {
    let Ok(tmux) = service.tmux() else { return vec![]; };
    let Ok(windows) = tmux.list_windows().await else { return vec![]; };
    let pattern = format!("review-pr-{pr_number}-");
    let mut killed = vec![];
    for w in windows {
        if w.window_name.contains(&pattern) {
            if let Err(e) = tmux.kill_window(&w.window_id).await {
                warn!(window = %w.window_name, error = %e, "failed to kill reviewer window");
            } else {
                info!(window = %w.window_name, "killed reviewer tmux window");
                killed.push(w.window_name);
            }
        }
    }
    killed
}

### 2. Rewrite live_reviewer_for_pr (handlers/agent.rs ~L1617)

Same pattern: scan tmux windows for review-pr-{N}- instead of .exo/agents/.
Return Some(window_name) if found, None otherwise.

### 3. Verify

cargo test -p exomonad-core -- cleanup_reviewer
confirm cleanup_reviewer_leaf returns non-empty cleaned_reviewers when a matching tmux window exists

