## Why not a split pane

A separate window keeps the Server window uncluttered and lets the user switch to Watcher on demand. Consistent with how process companions work.

## Why not killed by orphan reconciler

The orphan reconciler (reconcile_session_timeouts) kills agents by reading .exo/agents/{slug}/spawned_at. The Watcher window has no .exo/agents/watcher/ directory, so reconciler never touches it. No additional exempt-list needed.

## Dependency

Depends on issue #370 (watcher.log must be written). The window works without it (tail -f on an empty file) but shows no useful output until #370 lands.

